---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Data Protection & Healthcare Advertising Disclaimer"
  description="Data Protection and Healthcare Advertising Disclaimer for BBK Marketing Solutions LLC."
  effectiveDate="September 20, 2026"
  updatedDate="September 20, 2026"
>
  <p>
    {site.legalName} (&ldquo;BBK Marketing,&rdquo; &ldquo;BBK,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us,&rdquo; or
    &ldquo;our&rdquo;) provides specialized marketing and participant recruitment services for Clinical Research
    organizations.
  </p>
  <p>
    {site.rps.name} (&ldquo;{site.rps.shortName}&rdquo;) is a branded participant recruitment platform and service
    operated by {site.legalName}.
  </p>
  <p>
    This notice explains how BBK approaches participant recruitment, health-related information, advertising
    technologies, preliminary pre-screening, and data protection.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Our Role in Clinical Research Recruitment</h2>
  <p>BBK may support Clinical Research recruitment through services that include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>recruitment advertising;</li>
    <li>participant registration;</li>
    <li>participant engagement;</li>
    <li>preliminary pre-screening;</li>
    <li>communication and follow-up;</li>
    <li>recruitment workflow management;</li>
    <li>structured referral of potential participants to authorized Research Sites.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    BBK does not practice medicine, diagnose medical conditions, provide medical treatment, determine final
    clinical eligibility, obtain Study informed consent, or enroll or randomize participants into clinical trials.
  </p>
  <p>
    Final Study-specific screening, medical verification, informed consent, eligibility determination, and
    enrollment remain the responsibility of the applicable Research Site and research team.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information We May Collect</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on the recruitment program, {site.rps.shortName} may collect information directly from prospective
    participants or their authorized parent/legal guardian, including:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>name and contact information;</li>
    <li>age or date-of-birth information when required;</li>
    <li>ZIP code or general recruitment location;</li>
    <li>preferred language and communication preferences;</li>
    <li>self-reported health conditions or diagnosis information;</li>
    <li>responses to approved preliminary pre-screening questions;</li>
    <li>research interests;</li>
    <li>participant permissions and consent records;</li>
    <li>campaign and referral information.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    {site.rps.shortName} is designed to collect only information reasonably necessary for recruitment, preliminary
    pre-screening, participant communication, and referral activities.
  </p>
  <p>
    BBK does not routinely request complete medical records, laboratory reports, diagnostic images, insurance
    records, Social Security numbers, or other information that is unnecessary for the preliminary recruitment
    process.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Participant-Reported Health Information</h2>
  <p>
    Information provided through {site.rps.shortName} is generally self-reported by the participant or their
    authorized representative.
  </p>
  <p>The collection of this information does not constitute medical diagnosis, medical verification, or clinical screening by BBK.</p>
  <p>
    Where verification of diagnosis, treatment history, laboratory values, medical records, or other clinical
    information is required for a particular Study, that verification is performed by the applicable Research
    Site unless otherwise expressly established through an approved workflow.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Preliminary Pre-Screening</h2>
  <p>
    {site.rps.shortName} may use Study-specific preliminary questions to help organize participant referrals and
    determine whether additional follow-up may be appropriate.
  </p>
  <p>Preliminary pre-screening does not establish Study eligibility.</p>
  <p>
    A participant who completes a {site.rps.shortName} pre-screening process may still be determined ineligible by
    the Research Site following final Study-specific screening.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Participant Data Access</h2>
  <p>Participant information is not made available to arbitrary Research Organizations.</p>
  <p>
    Payment for BBK recruitment services does not provide a Research Organization with access to BBK&rsquo;s
    general participant network or participant database.
  </p>
  <p>
    Participant-level information is made available only through an authorized recruitment or referral workflow
    and only to the Research Organization or Site associated with that referral, subject to the participant&rsquo;s
    applicable permissions and the requirements of the recruitment program.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Future Research Opportunities</h2>
  <p>
    Participants may be offered the option to receive information regarding future Clinical Research
    opportunities that may be relevant to their profile.
  </p>
  <p>Participation in future-opportunity matching is voluntary.</p>
  <p>
    Where BBK offers this feature, the participant&rsquo;s preference is recorded separately and may be changed or
    withdrawn through available account or support channels.
  </p>
  <p>Declining future research communications does not affect a participant&rsquo;s ability to complete an existing recruitment process.</p>

  <h2>7. Advertising Platforms and Sensitive Information</h2>
  <p>BBK may use advertising platforms such as Meta, Google, or similar services to promote approved Clinical Research recruitment campaigns.</p>
  <p>BBK seeks to minimize the collection of sensitive health information directly within third-party advertising environments.</p>
  <p>
    Detailed health-related questions and preliminary pre-screening are intended to occur within the controlled
    {site.rps.shortName} participant environment whenever practical.
  </p>
  <p>
    BBK does not intentionally transmit participant health-profile responses, diagnosis information, or detailed
    pre-screening answers to advertising platforms for behavioral advertising purposes.
  </p>
  <p>Public advertising and website analytics are operationally separated from authenticated participant health-profile workflows where appropriate.</p>

  <h2>8. Communications</h2>
  <p>Subject to the participant&rsquo;s applicable permissions and preferences, {site.rps.shortName} may communicate through:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>email;</li>
    <li>SMS;</li>
    <li>telephone;</li>
    <li>WhatsApp;</li>
    <li>platform notifications;</li>
    <li>other approved communication channels.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Communications may include registration assistance, reminders, preliminary pre-screening support, administrative information, and referral coordination.</p>
  <p>Participants may change communication preferences or opt out of applicable communications through the methods provided in the message, platform, or by contacting BBK.</p>

  <h2>9. Parents, Guardians, and Pediatric Recruitment</h2>
  <p>{site.rps.shortName} does not permit children to independently create participant accounts where a parent or legal guardian is required.</p>
  <p>For pediatric research opportunities, the parent or legal guardian manages the account and provides information on behalf of the potential participant.</p>
  <p>The Research Site remains responsible for Study-specific parental permission, assent when applicable, informed consent, and clinical eligibility procedures.</p>

  <h2>10. Data Security</h2>
  <p>
    BBK uses reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards designed to protect participant
    and client information against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, loss, or misuse.
  </p>
  <p>Safeguards may include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access controls;</li>
    <li>role-based permissions;</li>
    <li>authentication controls;</li>
    <li>encrypted network communications;</li>
    <li>audit logging;</li>
    <li>restricted participant-data access;</li>
    <li>controlled storage;</li>
    <li>backup and recovery practices;</li>
    <li>security monitoring;</li>
    <li>vendor and access management.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>No electronic system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>

  <h2>11. HIPAA and Other Health Privacy Requirements</h2>
  <p>
    Health-related information may be subject to different federal or state privacy requirements depending on how
    the information is collected, used, disclosed, and the relationship between the parties involved.
  </p>
  <p>
    BBK does not rely on a blanket representation that all information handled through {site.rps.shortName} is, or
    is not, Protected Health Information under HIPAA.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where HIPAA or another applicable health-privacy requirement applies to a particular workflow or relationship,
    BBK will address the applicable requirements through the appropriate operational and contractual framework.
  </p>
  <p>
    Regardless of the legal classification of a particular data element, BBK treats identifiable participant health
    information as sensitive information and applies controlled-access and data-protection practices to its
    handling.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>BBK retains participant and recruitment information only as reasonably necessary for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>active recruitment activities;</li>
    <li>participant account functionality;</li>
    <li>authorized future research opportunities;</li>
    <li>referral documentation;</li>
    <li>legal, regulatory, audit, security, or contractual requirements.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Retention periods may vary depending on the type of information, the applicable recruitment program, participant preferences, and legal obligations.</p>
  <p>Information may be deleted, de-identified, restricted, or archived when it is no longer required for an authorized purpose.</p>

  <h2>13. Security Incidents and Breach Response</h2>
  <p>BBK maintains procedures for evaluating suspected unauthorized access, disclosure, loss, or misuse of participant information.</p>
  <p>Where applicable law requires notification of an incident or breach, BBK will provide the required notifications in accordance with the applicable legal framework.</p>

  <h2>14. No Sale of Participant Information</h2>
  <p>BBK does not sell participant medical or health information.</p>
  <p>BBK&rsquo;s clients purchase recruitment and related professional services.</p>
  <p>They do not purchase unrestricted access to participant profiles or BBK&rsquo;s participant network.</p>

  <h2>15. Questions and Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions regarding participant privacy, health-related information, or data protection may be directed to:</p>
  <p>
    {site.legalName}<br />
    {site.address}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.privacyEmail}`}>{site.privacyEmail}</a><br />
    Website: <a href={site.url}>www.bbk-marketing.com</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    {site.rps.name}:<br />
    <a href={site.rps.url}>www.bbk-rps.com</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
